{
  "text": " My name is James Mermigus and I am a civil rights slash constitutional attorney. I have filed over 150 individual lawsuits on behalf of firemen and policemen and some teachers as well. In addition, I have a few class actions also pending against the city of New York. I was successful in filing temporary restraining orders on behalf of all my clients and getting them stays of their termination until the article 78 proceeding was decided. And basically I'm going to be discussing the procedure where you could appeal a panel decision. I mean this Eric Adams when he rescinded the mandate on February 10th, he was in a live interview the same day and said that he will feel the need to reinstate him in the future. So I do think that this is something that will come up again and I think it's important for lawyers to learn this type of law especially with all the COVID litigation that's happening now and that's going to happen in the future.",
